[{"id":"VRCE-5-19-1","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":19,"verse":1,"english":"Hearing those words of that terrible Rākşasa, Sītā, stricken with grief and of feeble voice, slowly replied.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.877,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-21-1"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5019001","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"2bf405b182ad25573302465e058d8c43b221b4c43294b2aa9894b8c880760d5e","compact":"c57f09a3f437a4dcce61ee465e828652e9895fe32b319ef25b7825b5bdd20591","nasal":"c57f09a3f437a4dcce61ee465e828652e9895fe32b319ef25b7825b5bdd20591"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-19-2","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":19,"verse":2,"english":"Racked with grief, engaged in asceticism and weeping, Sita began. to tremble. And that excellent damsel, devoted to her husband, began to think of him.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-21-2"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5019002","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"ed60cb54f92af9814bf1295079d8bfcf8489d6bfd556a0c70861350464057103","compact":"f31a2aabbfa752a928479e28bf56837f37eec3d40ed256ff3c0c2c70c5b63b70","nasal":"11baed59576560724296dbc41b7d84e148a2c18534f4b016d1bf6e94afe1bdd8"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-19-3","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":19,"verse":3,"english":"Placing a twig before, that one, of beautiful smile, said-\"Do you take back your mind from me and place it in your own wives.\"","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.82,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-21-3"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5019003","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"343e37d9bf6da98ad99d54b1199fbac0bf5ddd1dd1845ac03bdd2566fcc06060","compact":"13ca4b393d0e3e73d916e8a45ed14eec747cd11abfbdcd7f4f142a446e19af02","nasal":"1a2c26251ba8f42a017d773c3056af9312620ce6fc73911a2a8bf64620abdef4"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-19-4","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":19,"verse":4,"english":"Like to a sinner unworthy of praying for final emancipation, it dose not behove you to expect to come by me. Devoted to one husband I shall never perpetrate such an iniquitous act.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.679,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-21-4"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5019004","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"b98f52a06c246ca5c208440d3e8feb96d85d75c4676a29789c6abda19215cf7b","compact":"f9f4c60083ae5d40bed19a4eb99bcba7c431d19c264b1dadd33e48a3411c6081","nasal":"f9f4c60083ae5d40bed19a4eb99bcba7c431d19c264b1dadd33e48a3411c6081"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-19-5","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":19,"verse":5,"english":"I am born in a high and have been married in a pious family. Having accosted Rāvana thus, the well-known Vaidehi, turning her back, again spake to him, saying. \"I should not live with you since I am another's wife and chaste.\"","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.82,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-21-5"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5019005","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"7b0fea883bf8090ddd0ebde5f28b4474fb6dee0c4771afb07ffdbfe49d168ed3","compact":"814755e1be3e9c6dd0e23047e633b662067d07e1edfef7903c2c1d3dd5012320","nasal":"814755e1be3e9c6dd0e23047e633b662067d07e1edfef7903c2c1d3dd5012320"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-19-6","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":19,"verse":6,"english":"I am born in a high and have been married in a pious family. Having accosted Rāvana thus, the well-known Vaidehi, turning her back, again spake to him, saying. \"I should not live with you since I am another's wife and chaste.\" Have your eyes always on religion and do you follow in the track of piety. Like to yours own wives, others are worthy of being protected by you, O ranger of the night.","alignment":{"type":"split","confidence":0.463,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-21-5","DUTT-5-21-6"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5019006","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"04a09de83c5eeb7f045d7d94d4c953235e49c9675d9b4edcb27a23f95c71bd9f","compact":"ffb95e3a5b40efc725ac356e90e28172374ab8a3c617d9d3fd46d341a464c197","nasal":"ffb95e3a5b40efc725ac356e90e28172374ab8a3c617d9d3fd46d341a464c197"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-19-7","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":19,"verse":7,"english":"Have your eyes always on religion and do you follow in the track of piety. Like to yours own wives, others are worthy of being protected by you, O ranger of the night. Making an example of you, do you enjoy with your own wives. Forsooth those vicious-minded, those of agitated senses, who are not satisfied with their own wives, are brought to misery by others' wives.","alignment":{"type":"split","confidence":0.571,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-21-6","DUTT-5-21-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5019007","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"89d4edeb22e945aa0836069df7389d4c3c8240ce3a8ab530a0d66147a46bc59b","compact":"0847cb555985c34939f5218b67ef3d76b0dcb56fb0c106d0824d9e11e86e7e1f","nasal":"0847cb555985c34939f5218b67ef3d76b0dcb56fb0c106d0824d9e11e86e7e1f"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-19-8","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":19,"verse":8,"english":"Making an example of you, do you enjoy with your own wives. Forsooth those vicious-minded, those of agitated senses, who are not satisfied with their own wives, are brought to misery by others' wives.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.797,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-21-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5019008","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"fb0d11f4234334b65cd0968365cda12e13afe3091a0ce37965d663121a2b533f","compact":"00af3fe19918d1ffe6f551527ccb06fe0a9cfecd4a797ac6429510eb01218f70","nasal":"ea73180ecd25ec110758eb48e8173891377327eecf6b6ba30d2b79aefce8d60c"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-19-9","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":19,"verse":9,"english":"(Methinks) there are no pious men here and even if there be any you do not follow him since you had such an adverse understanding, against human practice and usage. Or the considerate people have spoken the truth, but you, for the destruction of the race of the Raksasas, considering that false, had not followed it.","alignment":{"type":"split","confidence":0.516,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-21-8","DUTT-5-21-9"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5019009","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"4b0974efb7d65f9e929e299187fc3789f3cbc7a484ff7c2880be3a7b91abae06","compact":"8a4144e6a1a8c6ff911b0f12a91da456fcb3e3783c5765317618fa92faa8fe77","nasal":"f962efb7193e4847d57dd1a0732c80d4a2c985ded9b54845734e68cdd9ef27ae"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-19-10","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":19,"verse":10,"english":"Wealth, kingdom and cities-all are brought to naught when they are placed at the hands of a vicious and illiterate king.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-21-10"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5019010","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"f320764ae6558136f9886a6facd50bf38793ac88215a497235b57cacfff04149","compact":"087672b2e3b23a9b223b9717ba1c9823e106ec07dd7931caac5e6df1b34c74ad","nasal":"f40756a80d1a2ad5baabda02f52e09a169abb1afb77a64e092fa7c433480d4a1"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-19-11","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":19,"verse":11,"english":"Obtaining you, (therefore) as her king and for your folly only, this city of Lankā, abounding in jewels, shall soon be ruined.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.917,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-21-11"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5019011","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"911cba7f82d85617505129369d890ab7c11cad33bb2fdeeacc37f420ad534411","compact":"50020d3ad09fa1f8096e17784a630306a852a8668b9e909c4dde6381f7494134","nasal":"2cea64dbc01f1e13d54df53420467ff9bc8a3673ce89b8b10d65903a5f29d8b3"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-19-12","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":19,"verse":12,"english":"O Rāvana, every one delight in the destruction of that inconsiderate being, who bring about his own destruction and is engaged in the perpetration of evil deeds.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-21-12"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5019012","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"73d4f6b657f88275f33900bdbb810fd86ed0d93e3c345481add6dd35c3923210","compact":"4423fdd38a6ed1b8ccc3907098ae580fb6f0251ee4b88872e5b920d487a7e611","nasal":"a6d9c9de03addbde920f632568814472c8d09a0283a5002c4a24afabb4f2d008"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-19-13","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":19,"verse":13,"english":"In this way, yourself, the perpetrator of vicious acts, meeting with your end, those persons who had been tyrannised by you, shall, delightedly, say, “Oh! blessed are we since this terrible (Raksasa) has met with his end.\"","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-21-13"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5019013","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"cd3abcfa8e5b377e5879852d7474635ef91b419221455a01d0d128a1007a6064","compact":"cf941082387b1631025d3f382798e638ef3ff76e0c7104f49367fc73984cbb2f","nasal":"5ee5c63163474e89fcbacf124c5d4664f140ff703c2a666174d3731d8adfc17b"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-19-14","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":19,"verse":14,"english":"With wealth or riches you shall not be able to tempt me. As the rays of the sun belong to him, so I am Rāghava's only.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.857,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-21-14"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5019014","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"cb85e0f69dc29d4c23d7b8b9b4ac02af441240c1b38995b7e8ec496c26b54d75","compact":"7d0725db4b82c96cf446a5583d5d66700581e491155781c555d168ea89b719e3","nasal":"7d0725db4b82c96cf446a5583d5d66700581e491155781c555d168ea89b719e3"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-19-15","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":19,"verse":15,"english":"Having laid my head on the beautiful arms of that lord of men, how shall I place it again on another's?","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-21-15"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5019015","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"898005bdf4d23b33e67156b405acd174c445bbf2dbeff927bf3cc7f9ccae1666","compact":"156cc893f61e792a40f9101363cccc46c612343da7fc588ff86a2f3bdb2847de","nasal":"156cc893f61e792a40f9101363cccc46c612343da7fc588ff86a2f3bdb2847de"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-19-16","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":19,"verse":16,"english":"Like the knowledge of one God monopolized by the Brāhmaṇas only, I am the spouse of that lord of earth only, cognisant of higher truths and marrying me according to the pious ceremonials.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.639,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-21-16"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5019016","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"7241c53ca02b76724ee2536876543e672824e302f8c244e8ad76ba24ad750a9c","compact":"b2d912beab010a9f0163af5c0d159fe4b492af381134a3b281ce7fc5dc4a5460","nasal":"b2d912beab010a9f0163af5c0d159fe4b492af381134a3b281ce7fc5dc4a5460"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-19-17","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":19,"verse":17,"english":"to May good betide you, O Rāvaņa. Do you take me to Rāma, stricken with grief as I am, like to a she-elephant anxiously waiting in the forest brought to the lord of elephants.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.855,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-21-17"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5019017","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"dc7c420dd7258bdb7a727864bdbb994ee2cfe6a8b3a9bbd82204572e1e846e36","compact":"623a0df91d23ce903bdcc2646d21dc9ad0dbe422c9bf5cb9fd0c9c9efa125645","nasal":"623a0df91d23ce903bdcc2646d21dc9ad0dbe422c9bf5cb9fd0c9c9efa125645"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-19-18","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":19,"verse":18,"english":"It behove you to make friends with Rāma, that best of men, if do you desire to maintain your empire and do not wish to bring about your own destruction.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.774,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-21-18"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5019018","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"69d0d0a19a67cfaf929d0c50bfe74f4cf5633f40c23e493e45baa5475c5d7d3d","compact":"53e818109444efe04eb9157beadb552bd7250edca83dc31614d7c4b78f45daa0","nasal":"53e818109444efe04eb9157beadb552bd7250edca83dc31614d7c4b78f45daa0"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-19-19","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":19,"verse":19,"english":"Thunderbolt, even, when hurled, may leave you, Death himself may overlook you-but there is no safety for you, if Rāghava, the lord of men is enraged.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.897,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-21-22"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5019019","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"5970276861eee4df00b8d2488d5d9f99af3a7b003138910db0ca757c3eafaa9d","compact":"df22947e4dfc7bae255ce315e9f642170343dff295b307fe8f1f6e4ad5ffef50","nasal":"7d26ca3f2b837930391f82e3a72dabe7062b31580f3a52e28d505e26401bf7b6"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-19-20","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":19,"verse":20,"english":"You shall hear the terrible sound of the twang of Rāma's bow, like to the sound of the thunderbolt hurled by Indra. Soon shall arrows, bearing the names of Rāma and Lakşmaņa and having fiery heads like those of snakes, alight here.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-21-23"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5019020","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"1795c8efcd83a2ceaedd8bc84a0d6a792464e655b5410221b6ec3a7a5b123233","compact":"53d3b529fc478c27b1daf8311f79620624792bea195872b608caa1cacfd47405","nasal":"53d3b529fc478c27b1daf8311f79620624792bea195872b608caa1cacfd47405"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-19-21","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":19,"verse":21,"english":"You shall hear the terrible sound of the twang of Rāma's bow, like to the sound of the thunderbolt hurled by Indra. Soon shall arrows, bearing the names of Rāma and Lakşmaņa and having fiery heads like those of snakes, alight here.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.951,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-21-23"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5019021","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"521a41ff8d85b130a199603d067af821694e21a54fa917b6180ddb7c49ba61cc","compact":"64fd25fc578cba3a0761531a710327ac3ac